      \"line\": 747,
      \"body\": \"**MUST-FIX**: This fallback assigns any event without a matching iteration key to the *first* iteration. In real active sessions, iteration "'`N` events can exist before `context-iter-N.json` is written, so those events are currently mis-bucketed into iteration 1. That makes AC-2 summaries incorrect. Please derive buckets from the union of context iterations and event-declared iterations (and handle unscoped lifecycle events explicitly) instead of defaulting to iteration 1."
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/session-log-show.test.ts",
      "line": 160,
      "body": "**SHOULD-FIX**: This fixture gives `session.start` an `iteration`, but production session start/end events are unscoped. That hides the mis-bucketing bug in `computeIterationSummaries()`. Please add a regression case where context files are `[1,2]` and events include iteration `3` (or unscoped lifecycle events), and assert they are not counted under iteration 1."
